(Sleep and Memory Report \(APA 7 Structured Sections\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Title Page) Tj
T*
(Sleep, Cueing, and Recall Performance in a 2x2 Between-Participants Study) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Introduction) Tj
T*
(Sleep is often associated with memory consolidation, while targeted memory reactivation \(TMR\)) Tj
T*
(is hypothesized to improve recall beyond control conditions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Study Summary) Tj
T*
(Dataset size: N = 80 participants.) Tj
T*
(Design: 2x2 between-participants factors: Sleep \(Sleep vs Wake\) and Cue \(TMR vs Control\).) Tj
T*
(Outcome: recall_score \(0 to 40\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Method) Tj
T*
(Participants completed a word-pair learning and recall task under assigned sleep and cue conditions.) Tj
T*
(This report contains descriptive statistics only; no inferential claims are made.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
